(7654783, 1245433, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by the_rkp:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> not quite buying the light from the window. something about the intensity and direction of it doesn''t feel right. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>It''s a very very very strong light bulb :-P<br/>Jokes apart, I did it on a purpose, expecially to give a more "fantasy" look to the picture. What I do not understand is how some submissions totally "not extended" can be "rewarded" by the voters in these kind of contests... ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>hey Riccardo  .. just happened on this image .. and saw your comment .. <br/>i think the general idea is that ppl can do extended editing in a challenge like this .. but its not required .. it allows ppl to get crazy and combine images .. and feed their imaginations .. which would be impossible in a standard edit .. <br/>but if you can satisfy the challenge subject doing a standard edit thats perfectly ok too .. <br/>you could think of it like a speed limit .. say the limit is 100km/hr .. (i live in australia so its not miles/hr here) .. anyway .. limit 100km/hr .. but you can go slower if you like ... :)<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by the_rkp: Originally posted by posthumous: not quite buying the light from the window. something about the intensity and direction of it doesn''t feel right.  It''s a very very very strong light bulb :-PJokes apart, I did it on a purpose, expecially to give a more "fantasy" look to the picture. What I do not understand is how some submissions totally "not extended" can be "rewarded" by the voters in these kind of contests... ;-)   hey Riccardo  .. just happened on this image .. and saw your comment .. i think the general idea is that ppl can do extended editing in a challenge like this .. but its not required .. it allows ppl to get crazy and combine images .. and feed their imaginations .. which would be impossible in a standard edit .. but if you can satisfy the challenge subject doing a standard edit thats perfectly ok too .. you could think of it like a speed limit .. say the limit is 100km/hr .. (i live in australia so its not miles/hr here) .. anyway .. limit 100km/hr .. but you can go slower if you like ... :)', '2020-03-03 00:19:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(7654784, 1245433, 67145, '<td valign="top">ps .. love the mysterious and dark theme .. and the person barely visible ..  and of course the excellent edit .. :)<br/>pps .. did you mean ''sweat'' as in perspiration or ''sweet'' as in sweet .. <br/>either could work .. like it could take a lot of hiking to get to your unattainable home and hence the sweat .. !! .. <br/>or your home looks very warm and inviting .. with a magic view btw .. altho difficult to get to .. hence sweet .. ;)</td>', 'ps .. love the mysterious and dark theme .. and the person barely visible ..  and of course the excellent edit .. :)pps .. did you mean ''sweat'' as in perspiration or ''sweet'' as in sweet .. either could work .. like it could take a lot of hiking to get to your unattainable home and hence the sweat .. !! .. or your home looks very warm and inviting .. with a magic view btw .. altho difficult to get to .. hence sweet .. ;)', '2020-03-03 00:25:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(7654786, 1245433, 124729, '<td valign="top">Thanks roz for your comments.<br/>Hmm yes, sorry, it was a typo, I meant sweet, sorry :-D<br/> <br/>Regarding the "Extended" topic, I will answer in a private message, I arlready had a debate on the forum, and I don''t wanto to annoy more the community with my ideas. ;-)</td>', 'Thanks roz for your comments.Hmm yes, sorry, it was a typo, I meant sweet, sorry :-D Regarding the "Extended" topic, I will answer in a private message, I arlready had a debate on the forum, and I don''t wanto to annoy more the community with my ideas. ;-)', '2020-03-03 04:53:38.000000', NULL, 0);
